From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:49:47 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Studio, the Workbench's Claude Code session as a
 chat for designers (behind a flag, off)

Studio (meridian.studio.enabled, or --enable-meridian-studio; off by
default) shows the Workbench's Claude Code terminals as a chat. The page
gets, only while it is on: each terminal's status, open questions and
recent steps with Mission Control's message; a session's transcript from
an offset; answers to its permission questions; the result site's Boost
(as it was, before/after, undo). A session started from Studio gets
Studio's rules (keep originals, plain words, ask before anything leaves
the computer) through --append-system-prompt. Off, nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
